Problem Statement:

Develop a contact management system in C++

using a circular doubly linked list, an array and a queue.

Contact details (ID, name, phone, email, slot number) are stored in the circular list.

Slots are managed using an array.

Deleted contacts are held in a queue,

and the oldest can be restored.

The system supports adding, deleting, searching,

forward and backward display, slot status and history.

It follows your Hospital problem statement line by line and matches your latest code (circular doubly linked list, array and queue):

Patient became contact, bed became slot, and discharge became delete.
“Re-admitted” became “restored”.
The details list is ID, name, phone, email and slot number, since your code stores email instead of age and disease.
